Nah. I was always (for the year and a half I played D+D with a group
of boys from high school who all wondered with great puzzlement what a
girl was doing in their group, which all my friends shunned) given to
understand that Chaotic Evil = evil for evil's sake. Thus, orcs would
be chaotic evil. They're bent and determined to bring destruction and
choas to the world, not for personal gain or even pleasure at
tormenting others (after all, a lot of them die in terrible ways in
their quest to do so) but just for the sake of Being Evil.

Lawful and Neutral Evil would be those characters that don't
necessarily want to see the world engulfed in flames, they're just out
for their own ends and don't care who gets in the way. (Lawful is more
inclined to abide by the rules of society than Neutral, but otherwise
they're pretty interchangeable.)

I should also point out that though Curufin's attack on Beren was
pretty nasty/sneaky, there was no law against it in Elven or Human
society AFAIK (after all, Middle-Earth of the Silmarillion period was
a pretty brutal time by all accounts.) Hence it wasn't a chaotic act,
just an evil one.

